IMPORT prelude

§ `Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill -- shared domain`

-- Ontology for the encoding of the Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety
-- Risk Assessment) Bill (2026 No 339-1, as introduced 24 August 2026).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, retrieved 2026-09-11 from the
-- New Zealand Legislation website. There is no copyright in New Zealand
-- legislation (Copyright Act 1994, s 27) -- see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- This module owns the nouns. Rule modules import these types and never
-- redeclare them. INERT STYLE. No field name contains an apostrophe: 's is
-- L4's projection operator.

§§ `Internet service -- clause 5`

-- The facts a clause 5 scope determination turns on. Limb (a) of cl 5(1) tests
-- accessibility, exchange between users, at least one specified feature, and
-- the absence of an excluded-service character. Limb (b) tests an AI companion
-- service. Limb (c) is a regulation-making hook.

DECLARE `internet service` HAS
    name                                                                              IS A STRING

    -- cl 5(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i)
    `is accessible by a person who is in New Zealand`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 5(1)(a)(ii)
    `enables the exchange of digital content between 2 or more users`                  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 5(2), definition of specified feature, limbs (a) to (e)
    `recommends digital content to a user based on information about that user`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `generates a continuously updated stream of digital content`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `displays information about how others have viewed or engaged with user content`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `enables a user to view or engage with digital content for a limited period`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a feature specified as a specified feature in regulations under section 62`   IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 5(2), definition of excluded service, limbs (a) to (h)
    `solely or primarily enables person-to-person messages, email, voice or video calls` IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables video gaming`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables access to music or podcasts on demand`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables access to reviews, technical support, or advice`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables professional networking or development`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in education services`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables access to or engagement in healthcare services`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely or primarily enables an activity specified in regulations under section 62` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 5(1)(b)(ii) and (iii)
    `displays or otherwise makes available digital content`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses artificial intelligence solely or primarily to simulate a personal connection` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 5(1)(c)
    `is specified as an age-restricted platform in regulations under section 62`       IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Person in relation to a platform -- clauses 6, 7 and 8`

-- The facts an operator determination turns on. cl 6(1) is the substantive test
-- (management or control of the operations of the platform in New Zealand).
-- cl 6(2) displaces it whenever the regulator has designated someone under cl 7:
-- the designated person is then "the only operator". cl 8 limits the reach of
-- the Act to platforms accessible from New Zealand.

DECLARE `person in relation to platform` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING

    -- cl 6(1)
    `manages or controls the operations of the platform in New Zealand`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 7(1)(b)
    `is an interconnected body corporate of an operator under section 6(1)`             IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 6(2) and cl 7(1)
    `a designation under section 7 is in place for the platform`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been designated by the regulator as the operator under section 7`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator is satisfied that designating this person promotes the purpose`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 7(2)(a) and (b)
    `designating provides certainty about who is and is not an operator`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `designating ensures this Act can be effectively enforced for the platform`         IS A BOOLEAN

    -- cl 8(b)
    `the platform is operated so as to enable a person who is in New Zealand to access it` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Specified liability acts -- clause 34(3)`

-- The nine paragraphs of cl 34(3). Each is routed to exactly one penalty tier
-- by cll 45 to 47; whether that routing is total and disjoint is one of the
-- questions this encoding exists to answer.

DECLARE `specified liability act` IS ONE OF
    `section 34(3)(a) -- failure to take reasonable steps under section 11`
    `section 34(3)(b) -- keeping personal information contrary to section 12(1)(a)`
    `section 34(3)(c) -- using or disclosing personal information contrary to section 12(1)(b)`
    `section 34(3)(d) -- inadequate assessment on a directed repeat under section 19`
    `section 34(3)(e) -- failure to comply with a direction to repeat under section 19`
    `section 34(3)(f) -- failure to provide a risk assessment to the regulator`
    `section 34(3)(g) -- failure to designate a responsible individual under section 18`
    `section 34(3)(h) -- failure to comply with a notice to disclose a warning`
    `section 34(3)(i) -- failure to comply with a corrective notice`

§§ `Penalty tiers -- clauses 45 to 47`

DECLARE `penalty tier` IS ONE OF
    `tier 1`
    `tier 2`
    `tier 3`
